### =====================================================================
### END-TO-END (Phase 5): stock shows up in product search, through the API gateway (port 8080)
###
###   vendor sets stock -> inventory-service (asks product-read-service: "is this my product?")
###        -> MySQL + outbox -> Debezium -> Kafka (grocery.inventory.events)
###        -> product-read-service -> Elasticsearch (availableQuantity, inStock, lowStock)
###
### Needs: infrastructure, auth-service, product-service, product-read-service, inventory-service,
###        api-gateway, and the connectors (scripts\register-connectors.ps1).
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Run the requests IN ORDER.
### "wait" steps: a change reaches search after about a second (eventual consistency).
### =====================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

@vendorToken = {{vendorLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@vendor2Token = {{vendor2Login.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@productId = {{newProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}


### 1. vendor1 (Fresh Mart, store 1) logs in
# @name vendorLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 2. vendor2 (Green Basket, store 2) logs in
# @name vendor2Login
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor2@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 3. The admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 4. vendor1 adds a new product (product-service)
# @name newProduct
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 3,
  "name": "Country Brown Eggs",
  "sku": "FM-DRY-004",
  "unit": "PIECE",
  "unitQuantity": 12,
  "price": 120.00,
  "discountPercentage": 0,
  "taxPercentage": 0
}


### 5. (wait) Customers find it, but it is NOT in stock yet: no stock record -> availableQuantity 0, inStock false
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=brown


### 6. vendor1 sets its stock to 30 (inventory-service checks the product with product-read-service first)
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantityOnHand": 30
}


### 7. (wait) Search now shows it in stock: availableQuantity 30, inStock true, lowStock false
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=brown&inStockOnly=true


### 8. Sold out: vendor1 sets the stock to 0 (StockChanged + LowStockDetected)
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantityOnHand": 0
}


### 9. (wait) Customers who hide sold-out products no longer see it -> empty page
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=brown&inStockOnly=true


### 10. ...without the filter it is still listed, as out of stock (inStock false, availableQuantity 0)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/{{productId}}


### 11. vendor1's product list (product-read-service) with stock: only low stock -> new product, 7 and 17
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products?lowStockOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 12. vendor2 cannot touch vendor1's product -> 404
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendor2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantityOnHand": 999
}


### 13. Goods arrive: vendor1 adds 24 units -> back in stock
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory/{{productId}}/additions
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 24
}


### 14. (wait) In stock again for customers: availableQuantity 24
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=brown&inStockOnly=true


### 15. The admin sees low stock across all stores (inventory-service)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/inventory?lowStockOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 16. Without a token the vendor inventory is closed -> 401
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/inventory


### 17. CLEAN UP: vendor1 deletes the test product (it leaves search; its stock record stays in inventory_db)
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
